posts.body:
Seems to me that the easiest way would be to just keep all the rumours in an array, and add or remove from it as necessary. So, when you first start the game, set up a list in one of your variables with the starting rumours (I'm storing mine in variable 3 here):
(All of these are Script event commands)
Code:
const array = ['hint 1', 'hint 2', 'hint 3'];
$gameVariables.setValue(3, array)
Then, when you talk to the NPC, they can have a Script that says:
Code:
$gameMessage.add($gameVariables.value(3)[0]);
$gameVariables.value(3).push($gameVariables.value(3).shift())
Which will display the first message in the list, and then cycle it to the end.
To add new messages to the list, you'd do:
Code:
$gameVariables.value(3).push('hint 4')
And to remove them from the list once you've completed a quest, you'd do:
Code:
const index = $gameVariables.value(3).indexOf('hint 2');
if (index > -1) {
  $gameVariables.value(3).splice(index, 1);
}
